From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] balloon: reclaim file cache/slab for balloon pages (reclaim
 larger, not just faster)

Stock balloon_page_alloc() uses __GFP_NORETRY: allocation fails fast and
only already-free pages end up in the balloon. A guest holding tens of
MiB of file cache / reclaimable slab therefore reports lots of "freeable"
memory to the host that the balloon can never take - the host can only
reclaim what is already free.

For overcommitted Firecracker hosts that want the balloon to take *more*,
not just converge faster:

- __GFP_NORETRY -> __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL, __GFP_NOMEMALLOC dropped in
  favour of __GFP_HIGH | __GFP_MEMALLOC. The allocator may now run
  direct reclaim (drop clean file cache, shrink reclaimable slab) AND
  dip into watermark reserves with priority to satisfy balloon
  allocations, but still fails instead of invoking the OOM killer
  when nothing is reclaimable. __GFP_NOWARN is kept to stay quiet
  under pressure.
- WARNING: dipping into reserves is the most aggressive setting - the
  guest keeps almost no safety margin while the host inflates hard.
  Keep a ~10-20 MiB slack in the host balloon target and
  deflate_on_oom so a spiking guest survives.

Effect: inflating the balloon now converts guest page cache into
host-reclaimable memory. A guest showing e.g. 30 MiB used + 70 MiB cache
can be ballooned down close to used + unreclaimable kernel instead of
leaving the cache resident on the host.

Blast radius: balloon_page_alloc() is only used by balloon drivers; this
image enables only virtio_balloon.

Tunable: revert this hunk to restore stock fail-fast behaviour.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 mm/balloon_compaction.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/balloon_compaction.c b/mm/balloon_compaction.c
index 123456789014..123456789015 100644
--- a/mm/balloon_compaction.c
+++ b/mm/balloon_compaction.c
@@ -120,8 +120,17 @@
  */
 struct page *balloon_page_alloc(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Maximum reclaim: allow direct reclaim (drop file cache, shrink
+	 * reclaimable slab) AND dip into watermark reserves with priority,
+	 * so the balloon can take cached memory plus almost everything
+	 * free. Still fails instead of OOM-killing when nothing is
+	 * reclaimable. WARNING: reserves are the guest's last safety
+	 * margin - keep host-side slack + deflate_on_oom.
+	 */
 	struct page *page = alloc_page(balloon_mapping_gfp_mask() |
-				       __GFP_NOMEMALLOC | __GFP_NORETRY |
+				       __GFP_HIGH | __GFP_MEMALLOC |
+				       __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL |
 				       __GFP_NOWARN);
 	return page;
 }

